{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LRE8F3QGRnbpTCj8r74u11","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the answer to your question.\\\\n\\\\n## Answer\\\\n\\\\n**Kirk True, the KIP-1324 author, confirmed on May 5, 2026 that failed push RPC retry targets a **different broker node**.**\\\\n\\\\nIn his response to Muralidhar Basani's question (mb-6) about RPC failure behavior, Kirk True explicitly stated:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"mb-6 : In general, if the rpc fails for one random node, will it retry to a different node?\\\\n>\\\\n> Yes, the retries should target a different broker node.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n**Source:** `/store/kips/KIP-1324/2026-05-05-067a5f19.md` (lines 69-72)\\\\n\\\\nThis is Kirk True's reply sent on May 5, 2026 at 14:47:53 UTC in the KIP-1324 (Support client configuration observability) discussion thread.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1324/2026-05-05-067a5f19.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1324/2026-05-05-2c5cceb2.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1324/2026-05-05-754ee8cf.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1324/2026-05-05-861ac2bd.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":21.12,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":2,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":104983,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":33124,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.0850243,\\\"input_tokens\\\":58,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1644}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8831e326-55f8-4d30-843c-a06641985c88","uuid":"de42d3b6-bc22-45e0-873c-083607362c08","timestamp":"2026-09-27T19:26:35.910Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the answer to your question.\\\\n\\\\n## Answer\\\\n\\\\n**Kirk True, the KIP-1324 author, confirmed on May 5, 2026 that failed push RPC retry targets a **different broker node**.**\\\\n\\\\nIn his response to Muralidhar Basani's question (mb-6) about RPC failure behavior, Kirk True explicitly stated:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"mb-6 : In general, if the rpc fails for one random node, will it retry to a different node?\\\\n>\\\\n> Yes, the retries should target a different broker node.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n**Source:** `/store/kips/KIP-1324/2026-05-05-067a5f19.md` (lines 69-72)\\\\n\\\\nThis is Kirk True's reply sent on May 5, 2026 at 14:47:53 UTC in the KIP-1324 (Support client configuration observability) discussion thread.\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1324/2026-05-05-067a5f19.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1324/2026-05-05-2c5cceb2.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1324/2026-05-05-754ee8cf.md\\\",\\\"kips/KIP-1324/2026-05-05-861ac2bd.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":21.12,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":2,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":104983,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":33124,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.0850243,\\\"input_tokens\\\":58,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1644}}\"}","_meta":{"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"{\"answer\":\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the answer to your question.\\n\\n## Answer\\n\\n**Kirk True, the KIP-1324 author, confirmed on May 5, 2026 that failed push RPC retry targets a **different broker node**.**\\n\\nIn his response to Muralidhar Basani's question (mb-6) about RPC failure behavior, Kirk True explicitly stated:\\n\\n> \\\"mb-6 : In general, if the rpc fails for one random node, will it retry to a different node?\\n>\\n> Yes, the retries should target a different broker node.\\\"\\n\\n**Source:** `/store/kips/KIP-1324/2026-05-05-067a5f19.md` (lines 69-72)\\n\\nThis is Kirk True's reply sent on May 5, 2026 at 14:47:53 UTC in the KIP-1324 (Support client configuration observability) discussion thread.\",\"error\":null,\"files\":[\"store\",\"kips/KIP-1324/2026-05-05-067a5f19.md\",\"kips/KIP-1324/2026-05-05-2c5cceb2.md\",\"kips/KIP-1324/2026-05-05-754ee8cf.md\",\"kips/KIP-1324/2026-05-05-861ac2bd.md\"],\"seconds\":21.12,\"truncated\":false,\"turns\":2,\"usage\":{\"cache_read_tokens\":104983,\"cache_write_